'' A PARAMETER WITH NO TYPE IS THE DEFAULT-TYPE FEATURE, and tiko-lang does not have
'' it. fbc, measured:
''
''     sub mysub( byval s$ )
''     error 147: Default types or suffixes are only valid in -lang deprecated or
''                fblite or qb
''
'' tiko left the parameter UNTYPED and carried on: it reached the emitter as
'' 'define void @"MYSUB"(void %p0)' and clang answered "void type only allowed for
'' function results". The N_VAR arm has reported this since TKO0320 was added -- its
'' comment even names 'byval s$' as an example -- and the PARAMETER path never did.
''
'' Both spellings are here: the suffix one, and the bare name, which is the same rule.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --emit-ir tests/diagnostics/src/param-no-type.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0320
'' EXPECT-NOT: void %p0
